WEBVTT

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.420
What's wrong, Alice?

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.150
You seem down.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.530
Oh, are those photos of England?

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.070
Talking to my mum on the phone yesterday made me think of home.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.780
Your "mum"?

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.330
That sounds tasty!

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.700
You mean your mother, right?

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.030
You must be homesick.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.750
Is that what you meant, Alice?

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.130
I understand.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.670
Starting today, I will be your mother.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.670
What?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.050
Alice...

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.010
I wonder how Poppy's doing.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:50.640
Who?

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.560
It's probably her dog's name.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.130
Woof!

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:55.890
Woof, woof!

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.560
Sorry for making you worry.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.640
I'm fine now.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:03.150
I feel much better.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.990
You're all here in Japan with me,

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.280
and every day is so much fun.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.990
Alice, you're such a good girl.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.240
Can I see your album?

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.330
Sure.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.500
Is this your mother, Alice?

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.500
Yes.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.170
She's so pretty.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.460
Maybe you take after your father...

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.370
What?

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.550
That's the first time anyone's said that to me.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.680
Who's this?

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.810
My friend from England.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.640
Your friend?

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.560
That's right.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.640
A <i>friend</i> ?

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.690
Y-Yes.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.060
I can't believe Alice has a friend back in England.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.860
That makes me a little sad.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.030
Why?

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.700
What's she like?

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.740
Her name is Karen.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.200
Her father is Japanese,

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.160
and she taught me how to speak the language.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.030
I see.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.270
If you ever meet her, I'm sure you two will become friends, Shino.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.900
Alice's blonde friend.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:03.920
If we became friends...

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.820
I'd have a girl on each arm!

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.470
She's back to her usual self.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.340
Thank you for showing us your photos.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.930
We enjoyed looking at them.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.180
I hope you'll all show me your photo albums sometime.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.680
No way!

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.020
What's wrong with you?

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:27.410
Oh, sorry, but there are naked pictures of me in mine!

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.070
From when you were a baby!

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.070
The rain's stopped.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.780
You're right.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.620
Maybe it was the rain making you nervous.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.480
Maybe.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.540
It's a rainbow!

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.680
England's on the other side of that rainbow!

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.690
What a poet...

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.060
Those boots...

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.410
It feels like I've seen a lot of foreigners around lately.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.280
Maybe you just started noticing them more since Alice arrived.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.160
Now that you mention it,

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.210
I met a blonde girl around here the other day.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.080
What?

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.670
Tell me all about it!

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:52.050
Well, she wasn't very tall.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:55.170
She was wearing a Union Jack jacket,

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:59.050
and she had straight blonde hair and grey eyes...

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.640
Right, she looked just like this.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.640
That <i>is</i> her, isn't it?!

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.280
What a beautiful blonde girl.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:08.810
Karen?

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.750
Alice.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:13.940
Alice! Alice!

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.570
Karen.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:20.740
Who are you?

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:22.830
Shino, you've got nothing to do with this!

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.580
My name is Kujou Karen.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.790
It's Alice's friend from that photo.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.000
Alice said she was half-Japanese, right?

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.380
Karen, what brings you to Japan?

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:38.840
Zoom, zoom!

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.470
It's a long story.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.810
<i>Isn't Alice here?</i>

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:51.600
<i>Well, Alice has gone to Japan to study.</i>

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:53.610
<i>Japan?</i>

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.400
<i>Dad, what's Japan like?</i>

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.470
<i>Japan's a great place.</i>

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.160
<i>It's my home.</i>

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.220
<i>I know.</i>

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.540
<i>Why don't we all go live in Japan for a while?</i>

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.170
And that's what happened.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.920
Just like that?

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.960
Blonde hair...

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.400
Shino, we need to get to school.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.760
You're right...

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.680
Starting today, I'm one of your school friends.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.100
That uniform...

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.060
Now that I look at it, that's our school uniform.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.400
That's exactly what it is!

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.900
I transferred!

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.800
<i>S-Shino is...</i>

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.840
It's too bad Karen's in a different class.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.380
Let's go see her later.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.220
I can't wait for lunchtime!

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:11.940
Huh?

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:14.230
Alice, you seem down.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:15.860
N-No, I'm not at all.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.150
Alice!

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:21.400
Alice, I'm here!

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.320
Karen, your Japanese has improved.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.410
I studied hard every day.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.660
Karen, did you grow up in England?

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.580
Your speech sounds a bit broken, for a half-Japanese.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:33.710
Yes.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.380
My father normally spoke in English.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.420
I want to become fluent in Japanese, like Alice.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.070
Broken Japanese is better.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.180
It's cute.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.740
I still have long way.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:49.680
Japanese very hard!

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.960
<i>That sounded intentional.</i>

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.720
By the way,

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:56.270
lots of half-Japanese kids have names that work in Japanese,

00:07:56.270 --> 00:08:00.010
as well as foreign languages, like Risa and Naomi.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.080
My father named me.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.410
In kanji, my name is written as "lovely flower."

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.030
What a beautiful name.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:13.800
He probably named you in the hope that you'd grow up to be a lovely girl.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.370
Shino, what about my name?

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:21.670
Your name means you will grow up to be small and cute like a squirrel.

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:22.830
A squirrel, huh?

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:23.880
I see.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:26.010
Her name isn't <i>A Risu</i>, you know.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:30.720
Youko, Shinobu, and... um...

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:31.760
It's Aya.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.020
Ayaya?

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.930
It's not that long.

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:35.690
Just Aya.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.230
Ayaya! Ayaya!

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.650
Ayaya!

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:45.400
Ayaya! Ayaya! Ayaya!

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:46.890
Karen,

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.870
please call me Shino.

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:53.580
It's what my friends call me.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.930
Shino, are you a ninja?

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.290
Can you walk up walls?

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.000
Oh yeah, like "shinobi".

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:02.670
I don't know about that...

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:03.320
What?

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:04.380
You can't?

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.920
Of course she can!

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.180
Shino is so amazing, she can do anything!

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:09.510
What?

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:10.760
Come on, Shino.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.140
Walk up the wall!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:13.890
You want me to do what?!

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:15.730
What's wrong, Alice?

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.060
You're acting strange.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:17.760
What?

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:19.440
What do you mean?

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.110
You're jealous of Karen, aren't you?

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:24.910
Is that true?

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:29.950
It's true that Karen is of average height,

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:34.370
and the way she talks is more foreign and more appealing.

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:38.250
But you have many strengths of your own, Alice.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.460
Have confidence in yourself!

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:47.470
That's not going to make her feel any better, Shino.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:52.600
Alice?

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:53.600
Karen?

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:58.180
Karen, I'm sorry for coming to Japan without telling you.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.940
I really wanted to study here.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:02.860
And I wanted to see Shino...

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:07.570
There was something that kept bugging me.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:09.580
That promise we made when we were little.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.240
That's why I followed you to Japan.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.700
Promise?

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:16.830
That's right.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:22.590
I wanted to return the pencil I borrowed from you.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.210
Thanks...

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.840
No one cares about a pencil!

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.550
I live that way.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:32.260
Okay.

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:33.140
See you later.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:34.670
See you tomorrow.

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:35.260
See you...

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:36.850
See you tomorrow.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:39.940
A foreigner!

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:41.300
She's a foreigner!

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:42.150
Karen!

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:45.960
Japanese people just wave when they say goodbye!

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:46.690
Geez!

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:49.530
Oh, I see.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:50.820
Alice.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.240
Japan is so cool.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:58.660
Yeah.

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:00.830
Have you already tried natto?

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:04.330
They sometimes speak to each other in English.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:06.660
That's amazing!

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.090
There's something different about the two of them.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.220
I know what you mean.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:12.800
They look like celebrities!

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:14.430
Maybe I'll ask for their autographs.

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.140
Me, too.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.310
Why?

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:35.740
I wonder what they're talking about.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.490
So cool.

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:55.550
I slept really well.

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:59.310
Oh, really?

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:18.780
I want to be friends with my classmates,

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:20.700
but it isn't going so well.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.500
You only just transferred here, after all.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.330
It might be difficult for them to talk to you just because you're a foreigner.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:32.670
You may be half-Japanese, but you look like any other foreigner.

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:33.850
Huh?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.590
Shino, what about me?

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:38.370
If you were to compare them to animals, Karen would be...

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:42.330
A lion in a herd of deer.

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:45.390
I must flee...

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:47.900
Shino, that's not a good analogy.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:53.320
Come to think of it, Aya-chan transferred here, too.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:56.030
You moved here in your first year of middle school, didn't you?

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:57.700
Y-Yeah.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.740
Oh, so you're my senpai!

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:03.290
Please give me advice on making friends with my classmates.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:06.790
W-Well, the most important thing is...

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:10.550
to read the situation.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:13.500
Oh, like a weathervane.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.630
You need to read the situation, not the wind.

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:23.010
<i>My name is Oomiya Shinobu.</i>

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:26.520
<i>Would it be all right if I called you Aya-chan?</i>

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:29.190
<i>S-Sure, if you like.</i>

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:31.610
<i>Let me show you around the school.</i>

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:32.820
<i>Let's go.</i>

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:34.480
<i>D-Don't go out of your way for me.</i>

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.820
<i>The teacher gave me a map of the school.</i>

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:42.530
<i>Um, not that I don't want you to...</i>

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.240
The old wound...

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:46.450
Aya-chan, what's wrong?

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.250
I'm sorry I can't be of any help.

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:55.710
After that, Youko-chan dragged you around school, didn't she?

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.170
<i>Aya.</i>

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:00.470
<i>What are you doing on your own?</i>

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:00.950
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.130
<i>W-Well, um...</i>

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.720
<i>Oh, sorry.</i>

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:05.510
<i>I haven't introduced myself yet.</i>

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:07.950
<i>I'm Inokuma Youko.</i>

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.480
<i> Call me Youko.</i>

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:10.690
<i>O-Okay.</i>

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:11.900
<i>Nice to meet you.</i>

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:13.320
<i>Oh, I know!</i>

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:15.860
<i>I'll show you around the school.</i>

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.230
<i>Let's go.</i>

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:18.940
<i>What?</i>

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.070
<i>Are you free today?</i>

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:22.320
<i>U-Um, well...</i>

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:25.110
<i>Can I come to your house?</i>

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.750
That's right.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:34.710
She stuck with me until she got used to this school.

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:52.230
You were like an abandoned little puppy.

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:55.260
Liar!

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:56.570
Don't make up stories!

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:58.070
It's true.

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:00.280
They're good friends.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:02.280
I can see that.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.590
Repaying your debts.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:10.650
Happy and fulfilled.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.120
What are you talking about?

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.880
We've got to defend our honour as Japanese people.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.100
Um... Yakiniku meal.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:20.460
Heian period?

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:22.760
Those work.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:25.180
Such composed smiles...

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:26.680
We lost.

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:37.030
Sensei, show me how to do this one.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:38.730
Me, too!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.940
Hey, I was first.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:49.290
I ended up sleeping for 12 hours.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:50.770
That's way too long.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:54.750
Stare...

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:01.340
What are you doing, Karen?

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.260
Oh, Shino.

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:05.430
I see.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:08.760
You still aren't getting along with your classmates.

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:13.180
Maybe they don't want to talk to me because of my slanted eyes.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.880
You seem so gentle and approachable.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:16.770
I envy you.

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:20.690
It takes time for people to understand each other.

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:23.940
Your smile is wonderful, Karen.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:26.450
You might even make a hundred friends someday.

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:30.830
Everyone's so nice, and I love them all,

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:33.120
but I get the feeling you're special, Shino.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.210
You're making me blush.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:40.670
Hey, Alice.

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:41.590
Huh?

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:46.430
I didn't know you were there, Alice.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.980
I'm sure you'll fit right in with your class, Karen.

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.360
I hope so.

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.520
Fight!

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:01.940
What?

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.390
What are you talking about?

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:07.700
Karen, that's a cute jacket.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:08.950
It's my favourite.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.320
Isn't it against school rules?

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:17.670
Hey, Karen, why don't you join a club?

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:19.970
A club, huh?

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.040
Alice, are you in a club?

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:23.840
We're in the Going Home Club.

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:24.800
I'm in the Shino Club!

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:26.670
What's that?

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:30.760
It's a club where you talk to Shino and have lunch with Shino.

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:33.640
I'd like to join that club!

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.890
I-I'm the club president.

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:37.640
Really?

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.060
So it's basically just a fan club?

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:52.410
I feel a little better now.

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:56.500
I'm going to try talking to my classmates today.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.910
I'm sure they'll all become my friends.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.500
Karen!

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.830
You can do it.

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.050
Yes.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.300
That's everything.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:12.120
Does anyone else have anything to report?

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:13.180
Yes, yes, me!

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:15.260
Kujou-san?

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.090
Go ahead.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:16.810
What is it?

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:32.860
It's all right!

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.160
I'm unarmed!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:39.660
I came here from England,

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.790
but I'm a high school student just like all of you.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.540
I want to be your friend.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.300
Feel free to talk to me.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:49.800
I'll do my best.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:58.810
Huh?

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:08.730
Karen-chan, let's be friends.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:09.940
Me, too!

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:13.820
Everyone...

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:19.080
Nice job.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:19.950
Yeah.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.580
Karen's amazing, isn't she?

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.380
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:27.710
<i>Maybe we don't speak the same language,</i>

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:32.090
<i>but we can communicate as long as we try to listen to each other's hearts.</i>

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:36.140
Yeah, she sure is.

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:38.390
Thank you, thank you.

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:40.090
I can't wait to be your friend.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.760
Um, Karen-chan...

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.900
Bye-bye.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:46.940
Bye-bye!

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:48.650
See you tomorrow!

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.520
Everyone spoke to me.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:52.610
It was great.

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:53.990
That's good.

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:57.370
You've always had a bold personality, Karen.

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:00.660
But that's what I like about you.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:01.830
Thank you!

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:03.500
I love you too, Alice!

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.750
Karen, what about me?

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:08.070
Of course, I love you too!

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.060
Hey, Karen!

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.550
That's being <i>too</i> bold!

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:13.670
It looks like Alice is jealous again.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:17.090
I'm not jealous!

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.930
Okay, okay.

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:21.430
Bye-bye.

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:27.810
When we were in middle school,

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:29.980
if I had been a little bolder,

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:32.940
I wonder if I would have made friends with everyone right away, like Karen.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:40.030
Maybe, but the way you can think things
through with a cool head is your strength.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:40.820
What?

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:41.580
My...

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.620
At least your reactions are easy to read.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.080
S-Shut up!

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:52.250
You really were an innocent little girl back then.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.560
Come on, stop talking about that!

00:22:44.430 --> 00:22:47.790
Yesterday, I took a step towards becoming an adult.

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:48.680
Oh?

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:49.660
Congratulations.

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:51.000
Show a little interest!

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:52.080
Take the bait!

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:56.920
Yesterday, I went to a ramen shop and ate ramen all by myself.

00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:58.660
You went to a ramen shop by yourself?

00:22:58.660 --> 00:23:00.010
How mature!

00:23:00.010 --> 00:23:03.090
I can barely walk into fast food places by myself.

00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:10.310
One bowl of ramen, please!

00:23:10.310 --> 00:23:11.940
One ramen coming up!

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:14.440
Make it hot, please!

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:19.150
That's amazing in its own way!

00:23:19.150 --> 00:23:20.990
She's fearless!

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:23.950
Karen, you smell nice.

00:23:23.950 --> 00:23:25.560
It must be my shampoo!

00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:27.310
Shino, you smell nice, too!

00:23:27.310 --> 00:23:29.400
You smell like incense!

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:31.260
You smell like a dresser, too!

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:33.540
No, I don't! I don't really, do I?!

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:35.920
See you next time.
